Inspiration:
The inspiration for Recipe Vault came from having recipes scattered everywhere —
tucked into my computer's bookmarks, buried in notes apps, written on scraps of paper, or half-remembered from a YouTube video.
I wanted a single, dedicated place to save and organize recipes that I actually cook, something that felt personal
and pleasant to use rather than just another generic list.
My "Recipe Vault" project was built to solve that problem by keeping my recipes organized for easy access.

~~~~

Vision
The vision for Recipe Vault is to be a clean, user-friendly, elegant desktop recipe manager that
feels like a personal cookbook you actually enjoy opening. Rather than relying on an internet connection
or a subscription, all recipes are stored locally on your machine. The application vision includes:

- A full recipe library organized by cuisine type and searchable by ingredient or name
- Rich recipe cards with photos, prep/cook times, and serving sizes
- The ability to add, edit, and delete recipes through a polished, intuitive interface

~~~~

Basic Functionality

Recipe Vault currently supports the following core features:

- Browse recipes from a sidebar list view, with details displayed on the right panel
- Search recipes by name or ingredient using the live search bar
- Filter by cuisine (Italian, Japanese, American, Desserts, German, Chinese, French, Mediterranean, Other) via a dropdown menu
- Add new recipes through a dedicated second window, including name, cuisine, prep time, cook time,
  servings, ingredients, instructions, and an optional photo
- Edit existing recipes by selecting one from the list and opening the same Add/Edit window pre-populated with saved data
- Delete recipes with a confirmation dialog to prevent accidental removal
- View recipe photos alongside the details panel when an image has been uploaded
- Persist recipes between sessions — all data is saved to local .txt files in a recipes_data/ folder, and images are
  copied into a recipe_images/ folder


The application also includes keyboard shortcuts:

    CTRL + N = opens a window for adding a new recipe
    CTRL + E = opens a window to edit the selected recipe

